>> title: Japanese Beef Curry
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, japanese, curry, one-pot, potatoes
>> counters: Ramen Shop, One Pot, Japanese Home Cooking
>> aka: kare raisu, karē raisu, curry rice, Japanese curry
>> servings: 6
>> time: 2 hr 30 min
>> slack: forgiving — the roux goes in off the boil, because a curry roux boiled hard goes grainy and separates and will not whisk smooth
>> washing-up: the heavy pot
>> keeps: 3 days — the roux sets much thicker cold, so loosen it with water; the potatoes go grainy

Brown @beef chuck{2%lb}(900 g; cut in 1-in cubes), @kosher salt{2%tsp}, @vegetable oil{2%Tbs} in a heavy #pot{}.

Soften @yellow onions{2%large}(sliced), @carrots{2%large}(cut in chunks), @garlic{2%cloves}(grated) with @&(~1)browned beef{}.

>> step: simmer covered 1 1/2 hr
Simmer @&(~1)pot{} with @water{4%cup}(950 mL), @bay leaf{1} for ~{90%min}.

>> step: simmer 20 min more
Add @Yukon Gold potatoes{1%lb}(450 g; cut in chunks) to @&(~1)stew{} for ~{20%min}.

>> step: stir in the roux
Stir @Japanese curry roux{4%oz}(120 g; about half a 220-g box), @Worcestershire sauce{1%Tbs}, @soy sauce{1%tsp} into @&(~1)stew{} off the heat.
